                                                <property>
                                                    <name>toolTip</name>
                                                    <string>The function string understood is very similar to the C-syntax. The function have to be dependent on the variables x and z.More detailed informations could be found in the documentation folder (function parser). &lt;h1&gt;valid operators&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;table&gt; &lt;tr&gt;  &lt;td&gt;()&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td&gt;expressions in parentheses first&lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;  &lt;td&gt;-A&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td&gt;unary minus&lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;  &lt;td&gt;A^B&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td&gt;exponentiation (A raised to the power B)&lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;  &lt;td&gt;A*B  A/B  A%B&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td&gt;multiplication, division and modulo&lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;  &lt;td&gt;A+B  A-B &lt;/td&gt; &lt;td&gt;addition and subtraction&lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/table&gt;  &lt;h1&gt;valid functions&lt;/h1&gt;  abs(A), acos(A), acosh(A), asin(A), asinh(A), atan(A), atanh(A), ceil(A), cos(A), cosh(A), exp(A), floor(A), int(A), log(A), sin(A), sinh(A), sqrt(A), tan(A), tanh(A)  &lt;h1&gt;Examples of function strings&lt;/h1&gt; 1+2 &lt;br&gt; -sin(sqrt(x^2+z^2))</string>
                                                </property>
                                            </widget>
